#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:43
msgid ""
"image:norse/logo.webp[width=109,height=96,float=\"right\"] The northern "
"regions of the Old World suffer from extremes of climate and geography "
"unlike anywhere else. The dense dark forests, high barren mountains, icy "
"seas and long winter nights conspire to make life here both hard and short. "
"This cruel land known as Norsca is a home to the Norsemen – a race of men "
"that are as fierce, brutal and unforgiving as the landscape itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:57
msgid ""
"Because little grows upon the rocky soil of the North the Norsemen have "
"traditionally turned to the sea for their livelihood. Their Kingships and "
"Longships set out for the shores of Albion the coasts of the Old World and "
"even further afield bringing warriors to pillage and extort what they "
"require.  Occasionally they will trade with other races or hire themselves "
"out as mercenaries in return for goods but most of the time they will simply "
"fight to get what they want. It is said that the Norsemen love war-song and "
"ale but most of all they love war.  Old Worlders tell horrifying tales of "
"these berserk warriors from over the Sea of Claws looting and burning from "
"their dragon headed vessels and ravaging the northern coasts of The Empire "
"and Kislev."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:63
msgid ""
"The Norsemen are known as excellent sailors and fearless warriors given to "
"great voyages and adventures; the most wayward of the Norse raiders have "
"sailed as far as Ulthuan and The Southlands bringing home tales of strange "
"lands, immeasurable wealth and wild creatures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:70
msgid ""
"The Norsemen are famously fond of their ale, so much so that they’ve been "
"known to wage war to obtain a decent stock for the winter. However, some "
"Norsemen whenever they have more than the slightest drop of Mead go into a "
"berserk frenzy, where they feel no pain and fear nothing. A bit annoying in "
"the Mead Hall, but very useful on the battlefield."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "Norse army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$norse.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. 2: or be, remove at all
#. 4: some rewording of the siege attack
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[berserkers,†1]]1. Berserkers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:96
msgid ""
"Such is the eagerness to get into combat that a unit of Berserkers will "
"always use its initiative to charge an enemy if possible and can’t be given "
"orders instead. They’ll never use their initiative to evade. They can’t be "
"driven back by shooting and do not roll for drive backs. If victorious in "
"combat, they must pursue or advance where possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:100
msgid ""
"Berserkers are unaffected by enemies that cause terror in combat, so they do "
"not suffer the usual −1 Attack modifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[ulfwerener,†2]]2. Ulfwerener"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:103
msgid ""
"Unlike [.edit]#normal# infantry troops, the Ulfwerener are based facing the "
"short edge in the same way as cavalry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:107
msgid ""
"They receive an additional +1 Attack when they charge an enemy in the open "
"in the same way as monsters and chariots, and they may also pursue cavalry "
"and chariots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:110
msgid "The Ulfwerener stands can never support or be supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:114
msgid ""
"Because of their rather bestial nature, only characters with the Were Kin "
"Character upgrade may join units of Ulfwerener."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:116
msgid "Ulfwerener units can not take any magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[storm-giant,†3]]3. Storm Giant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[war-mammoth,†4]]4. War Mammoth"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:122
msgid ""
"As the Mammoth is so gargantuan, it uses a 40 × 60mm base, with the short "
"edge being the front."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:128
msgid ""
"It causes terror and may attack troops on ramparts with its trunk in the "
"same manner as a Giant. Alternatively, it may elect to batter a wall section "
"or gateway with its tusks in the same manner as a battering ram."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:137
msgid ""
"During a siege a Norse War Mammoth in base contact with a wall section "
"permits one Norse infantry unit to assault that wall section via the "
"Mammoth.  The infantry climb ladders and ropes at the rear of the Mammoth "
"and use boarding ramps and the like to assault the fortress walls.  This is "
"not quite as effective as assaulting from a siege tower, so the enemy only "
"counts as defended rather than in the open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:143
msgid ""
"If a unit assaults in this manner, then the War Mammoth may not attack with "
"its trunk or batter the walls; such action would result in attacking "
"friendly troops or bringing a wall section down from under them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:150
msgid ""
"If a War Mammoth has accumulated 6–9 hits by the end of the Shooting phase "
"or Combat phase and is no longer engaged in combat it is deemed to have been "
"badly hurt. Once a Mammoth is badly hurt then all accumulated hits are "
"discounted and its maximum Hits value and Attacks are halved for the rest of "
"the battle (to 5 Hits and 4 Attacks)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[valkyries,†5]]5. Valkyries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:152
msgid "Valkyries can fly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:156
msgid ""
"Valkyries will always use their initiative to charge an enemy if possible "
"and cannot be given orders instead. They will never use their initiative to "
"evade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:159
msgid ""
"Valkyries are unaffected by enemy that cause terror in combat and they don’t "
"suffer the usual −1 Attack modifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[were-kin,†6]]6. Were Kin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:163
msgid ""
"[.edit]#Any character may take# the Were Kin special mount.  It is not a "
"mount as such, more an upgrade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:166
msgid ""
"A unit that is joined by a character with the Were Kin upgrade causes terror "
"in its enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:170
msgid ""
"No terrain restriction apply for Were Kin – just treat the character as "
"having +1 extra Attack and causing terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[horn-of-resounding,†7]]7. Horn of Resounding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:173
msgid "A single shaman in the army may be given this chariot upgrade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:175
msgid "It gives the shaman +1 Attack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:180
msgid ""
"[.edit]#Once per battle, the Shaman may blow the horn, inspiring the units "
"around him to fight harder. He adds +1 to all his Command for a single turn "
"only, bringing it to 9.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "Norse spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "Aspect of Wulfen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:192
msgid ""
"_The Shaman turns the friendly unit into an illusive pack of monstrous "
"creatures entailing the fear in a hearts of enemies._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:196
msgid ""
"This spell can only be cast on any friendly unit within range regardless of "
"whether the Shaman can see it or not. The unit counts as causing terror for "
"the duration of the Combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thunder of Fo’Wor"
msgstr ""

#.  bolt, comma
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:205
msgid ""
"_A lightning bolt shoots from the Shaman’s outstretched arm, burning all in "
"its path._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:211
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:198
msgid ""
"Draw an imaginary line 30cm long from the Shaman’s stand in any direction "
"you wish. The line will pass through any intervening units but not beyond "
"terrain that would normally stop a missile shot, e.g. over the crest of a "
"hill, more than 2cm of woodland, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:221
msgid ""
"Each unit under the line takes three shooting attacks worked out in the "
"usual way. Note that this spell can easily affect several units and will "
"affect all units that fall beneath the line (including your own). Unengaged "
"units can be driven back by a Thunder of Fo’Wor as with ordinary shooting "
"(even including friends). Engaged units cannot be driven back by the Thunder "
"of Fo’Wor but carry over any hits scored into the first round of combat; any "
"hits scored count as having been struck in the combat itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "Eye of the Raven"
msgstr ""

#.  Tense
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:230
msgid ""
"_The Shaman sacrifices a sacred Raven over a mystical flame.  Ingesting the "
"ash that is quickly formed gives him visions._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:247
msgid ""
"The Norse player may re-roll a single D6 at any time during the rest of his "
"turn, through his opponents turn or in his following turn up to the end of "
"his next Command phase when the effect of the spell ends if the re-roll has "
"not already been used. The result of the re-roll cannot be changed in any "
"way or re-rolled again, for example with an Orb of Majesty, Banner of "
"Fortune or through other means. Likewise the re-roll from this spell cannot "
"be used to re-roll any dice that another re-roll has already been used on. "
"Nor can the reroll be used in the case of a blunder of a command roll, not "
"even mystical foresight can help avert such mishaps, but it can mitigate the "
"effects, so can be used to re-roll the dice roll on the blunder chart. For "
"example if the Norse player rolled for a command needing a roll of a seven "
"and rolled a five and a three, he could re-roll the dice that came up as a "
"five, hopefully rolling a four or less making it a successful command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:250
msgid "Only one Eye of the Raven spell may be in effect per turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:252
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spite of Low’Key"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:258
msgid ""
"_The Shaman makes a weird enchantment calling the gods to curse the enemy "
"with bad luck and failure._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:266
msgid ""
"All enemy characters within 30cm of the spell caster that roll a double have "
"those orders count as blunders. This works on all results, from a double "
"one, to a double five. As a result all doubles rolled not only blunder, but "
"as with all normal blunders, it counts as a failed order. The only exception "
"is the enemy general, as he cannot blunder. The spell lasts until the end of "
"enemy Command phase."
msgstr ""
